module

public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.EssentiallySmall
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Limits.Types.Limits
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.PreservesSheafification
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.LocalOnCover.Quasicoherence
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.ULiftUnit

/-!
# The two presentations of a sheaf of modules agree

A sheaf of modules on a ringed site is quasi-coherent when it is locally the cokernel of a
morphism between coproducts of copies of the structure sheaf, which is Stacks 03DL(6).  The
global half of that condition — being such a cokernel outright — admits two formalizations
whose index types live in different universes.

`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` states it through universal properties, with the
coproducts and the cokernel taken in the universe `max u v r` containing the objects, the
morphisms and the sections of the coefficient ring sheaf, after the module has been moved there
by `SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation`; no sheafification instance on the site is needed, and
the index types are bounded by that same universe.  Mathlib's `SheafOfModules.Presentation`
states it through `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`, as a family of global sections generating
the module together with a family generating the kernel of the resulting morphism from the free
sheaf of modules; there the index types live in the universe of the sections of the ring sheaf,
and sheafification of abelian presheaves on the site is assumed.

This file proves the two equivalent.  The forward implication is unconditional; the backward one
needs the site to be essentially small in the universe of the sections, which is exactly what
makes the global sections of a sheaf of modules a type in that universe and so available as an
index type for `SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections`.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.presentationRelationsHom` is the morphism between free sheaves of
  modules carried by a `SheafOfModules.Presentation`: the generators of the kernel, followed by
  the inclusion of the kernel.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isColimitCofanUliftForPresentationFree`: the universe lift of a free
  sheaf of modules is a coproduct of copies of the universe lift of the structure sheaf.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isColimitCokernelCoforkPresentation`: the universe lift of the
  presenting morphism of a `SheafOfModules.Presentation` is again a cokernel projection.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationHomEquiv` and
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationSectionsEquiv`: the universe lift of sheaves of
  modules is fully faithful, so a morphism from the lifted structure sheaf to a lifted module is
  the same data as a global section of the module.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isColimitCofanULift` reindexes a coproduct of copies of one object
  along `ULift`, and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.isColimitCokernelCoforkOfEpiComp` says that a
  cokernel projection stays one after its source is composed with an epimorphism.  Neither
  mentions sheaves of modules.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.hasGlobalPresentation_of_presentation`: **a sheaf of modules
  with a `SheafOfModules.Presentation` has a `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation`.**
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_presentation_of_hasGlobalPresentation`: **on a site that is
  essentially small in the universe of the sections of the ring sheaf, a sheaf of modules with a
  `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` has a `SheafOfModules.Presentation`.**
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.nonempty_presentation_iff_hasGlobalPresentation`: the two taken
  together.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.preservesColimitsOfShape_moduleULift`: raising the universe of the
  sections of a sheaf of modules preserves coproducts.  This is what makes the forward
  implication work, and it rests on
  `Stacks.SheafOfModules.preservesSheafification_uliftFunctor`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_generatingSections_of_isColimit_cofan`: a module that receives
  an epimorphism from a coproduct of copies of the lifted structure sheaf, indexed by any type
  at all, is generated by a family of global sections indexed in the universe of the sections of
  the ring sheaf — the index is replaced by the set of sections it names.

## Implementation notes

`SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation` and the functor
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.moduleULift` that raises the universe of the sections of a sheaf of
modules are the same construction: `Stacks.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation_eq_moduleULift`
and `Stacks.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap_eq_moduleULift_map` are both `rfl`.  The
functor is used wherever functoriality or a universal property is needed, and
`SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation` wherever the statement has to match
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation`.

**Why the universe lift preserves coproducts.** Coproducts of sheaves of modules are not
computed on sections: they are the sheafification of the coproduct of the underlying presheaves,
and `ULift` of a sheafification is not visibly a sheafification.  The route taken is that
`AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor` carries local bijections to local bijections, hence commutes with
sheafification (`Stacks.SheafOfModules.preservesSheafification_uliftFunctor`), so that
`CategoryTheory.sheafComposeNatIso` identifies sheafifying-then-lifting with
lifting-then-sheafifying; a colimit of abelian sheaves is the sheafification of a colimit of
presheaves, which gives the preservation statement for `CategoryTheory.sheafCompose` along the
lift, and from there for sheaves of modules because
`AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.toSheaf_preservesColimits` preserves and
`CategoryTheory.Limits.reflectsColimitsOfShape_of_reflectsIsomorphisms` reflects.  The same
statement for `AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor` is proved, privately and for a different arrangement
of universes, inside
`StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Sites.RingedLocalization.FlatPullbackExact`; the version here is
public and in the universes the presentation predicates use.

**Where the essential smallness is used, and only there.**
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.small_sections` turns `CategoryTheory.EssentiallySmall.{r} C` into
`Small.{r} N.sections`, and that is the single place the hypothesis enters: the index type of a
`SheafOfModules.GeneratingSections` must be a type in the universe of the sections of the ring
sheaf, while a global presentation indexes its generators by a type in the larger presentation
universe.  Generation is a property of the *set* of sections, not of the indexing, so the index
may be replaced by the range of the family inside the global sections, which is small as soon as
the global sections are.

**The relations descend with the generators, not separately.** After the index of the generators
is shrunk, the kernel being presented changes: the original relations present the kernel of the
morphism out of the coproduct indexed by the original type.  The comparison morphism `θ` from
that coproduct to the universe lift of the free sheaf of modules on the shrunk index is an
epimorphism, because every structural inclusion of the latter factors through it, and the
presenting morphism stays a cokernel after composing the source with `θ`
(`Stacks.SheafOfModules.isColimitCokernelCoforkOfEpiComp`).  So the original relation module
still surjects onto the new kernel, and the same replacement of the index applies to it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DE](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DE)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DO)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u v r a b

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C} {R : Sheaf J RingCat.{r}}

/-! ### The universe lift as a functor -/

/-- The universe lift appearing in `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` is the functor
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.moduleULift` on objects. -/
theorem uliftForPresentation_eq_moduleULift (M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{r} R) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} M =
      (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R).obj M := rfl

/-- The universe lift appearing in `SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` is the functor
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.moduleULift` on morphisms. -/
theorem uliftForPresentationMap_eq_moduleULift_map {M N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{r} R}
    (f : M ⟶ N) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} f =
      (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R).map f := rfl

/-- Raising the universe of the sections of a sheaf of modules is fully faithful, so a morphism
between two lifted modules is the lift of a unique morphism. -/
noncomputable def uliftForPresentationHomEquiv (M N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{r} R) :
    (M ⟶ N) ≃ (_root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} M ⟶
      _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} N) :=
  (moduleULiftFullyFaithful.{max u v r, r} R).homEquiv

/-- The equivalence of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationHomEquiv` sends a morphism to
its universe lift. -/
@[simp]
theorem uliftForPresentationHomEquiv_apply {M N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{r} R} (f : M ⟶ N) :
    uliftForPresentationHomEquiv M N f =
      _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} f := rfl

/-- A morphism from the lifted structure sheaf to a lifted sheaf of modules is the same data as
a global section of the module: the lift is fully faithful, and the structure sheaf is free of
rank one. -/
noncomputable def uliftForPresentationSectionsEquiv (N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{r} R) :
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit R) ⟶
      _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} N) ≃ N.sections :=
  (uliftForPresentationHomEquiv (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit R) N).symm.trans N.unitHomEquiv

/-- On an essentially small site the global sections of a sheaf of modules form a type in the
universe of the sections: the global sections are a limit over the site, and a limit over an
essentially small index category of types in that universe is again one. -/
theorem small_sections [EssentiallySmall.{r} C] (N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{r} R) :
    Small.{r} N.sections := by
  have : EssentiallySmall.{r} Cᵒᵖ := inferInstance
  have : HasLimitsOfShape Cᵒᵖ (Type r) := hasLimitsOfShape_of_essentiallySmall.{r} Cᵒᵖ (Type r)
  exact (Types.hasLimit_iff_small_sections
    (N.val.presheaf ⋙ CategoryTheory.forget AddCommGrpCat.{r})).mp inferInstance

/-! ### Two pieces of general category theory -/

/-- Reindexing a coproduct of copies of a single object along `ULift`. -/
noncomputable def isColimitCofanULift {D : Type*} [Category D] {I : Type a} {O Pt : D}
    {ι : I → (O ⟶ Pt)} (h : IsColimit (Cofan.mk Pt ι)) :
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk (f := fun _ : ULift.{b} I => O) Pt fun j => ι j.down) :=
  Cofan.IsColimit.mk _ (fun s => Cofan.IsColimit.desc h fun i => s.inj (ULift.up i))
    (fun s j => Cofan.IsColimit.fac h (fun i => s.inj (ULift.up i)) j.down)
    (fun s _m hm => Cofan.IsColimit.hom_ext h _ _ fun i =>
      (hm (ULift.up i)).trans (Cofan.IsColimit.fac h (fun i => s.inj (ULift.up i)) i).symm)

/-- **A cokernel projection stays one after composing its source with an epimorphism.** If
`b : P ⟶ M` is a cokernel of `a : Q ⟶ P` and factors as `θ ≫ π` with `θ` and `π` epimorphisms,
then `π` is a cokernel of `a ≫ θ`.

A morphism out of `P'` killing `a ≫ θ` becomes, after composing with `θ`, a morphism out of `P`
killing `a`, hence factors through `b = θ ≫ π`; since `θ` is an epimorphism the factorisation
descends to `P'`. -/
noncomputable def isColimitCokernelCoforkOfEpiComp {D : Type*} [Category D] [HasZeroMorphisms D]
    {Q Pt Pt' M : D} {a : Q ⟶ Pt} {b : Pt ⟶ M} {θ : Pt ⟶ Pt'} {π : Pt' ⟶ M}
    (hab : a ≫ b = 0) (hb : IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ b hab)) (hfac : θ ≫ π = b)
    [Epi θ] [Epi π] (h : (a ≫ θ) ≫ π = 0) :
    IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ π h) := by
  refine CokernelCofork.IsColimit.ofπ' _ _ fun {T} k hk => ?_
  have h1 : a ≫ θ ≫ k = 0 := by rw [← Category.assoc]; exact hk
  obtain ⟨k', hk'⟩ := CokernelCofork.IsColimit.desc' hb (θ ≫ k) h1
  have hk'' : b ≫ k' = θ ≫ k := hk'
  refine ⟨k', (cancel_epi θ).mp ?_⟩
  rw [← Category.assoc, hfac, hk'']

/-! ### The universe lift preserves coproducts -/

/-- **Raising the universe of abelian groups commutes with sheafification**: it carries local
bijections to local bijections, because `ULift.up` is injective and hits every lifted section.
This is the input that makes the universe lift of sheaves of modules preserve coproducts. -/
theorem preservesSheafification_uliftFunctor (J : GrothendieckTopology C)
    [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{r}]
    [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r}] :
    J.PreservesSheafification AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor.{max u v r, r} := by
  refine ⟨fun P Q φ hφ => ?_⟩
  show J.W (Functor.whiskerRight φ AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor.{max u v r, r})
  rw [J.W_iff_isLocallyBijective] at hφ ⊢
  obtain ⟨hι, hσ⟩ := hφ
  refine ⟨⟨fun {U} x y h => ?_⟩, ⟨fun {U} x => ?_⟩⟩
  · have h' := Presheaf.equalizerSieve_mem J φ x.down y.down (congrArg ULift.down h)
    convert h' using 1
    ext V f
    exact ULift.up_injective.eq_iff
  · have h' := Presheaf.imageSieve_mem J φ x.down
    convert h' using 1
    ext V f
    show (∃ t : ULift.{max u v r} (P.obj _),
      ULift.up (φ.app _ t.down) = ULift.up (Q.map f.op x.down)) ↔ _
    simp only [ULift.up_inj, ULift.exists]
    rfl

/-- Sheafification of abelian groups in the universe `max u v r` exists and computes the local
bijections, as the instances the universe lift of sheaves of modules needs. -/
private theorem hasSheafify_and_wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat (J : GrothendieckTopology C) :
    HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r} ∧
      J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r} :=
  ⟨GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat.{max u v r, v, u} J,
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat.{max u v r, u, v} J⟩

variable [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{r}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{r}]

/-- Raising the universe of the sections of an abelian sheaf preserves coproducts: a coproduct of
abelian sheaves is the sheafification of the coproduct of the underlying presheaves, the lift
commutes with sheafification, and it preserves coproducts of presheaves because it does so
objectwise. -/
theorem preservesColimit_sheafCompose_uliftFunctor (I : Type r)
    (F : Discrete I ⥤ Sheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{r}) :
    PreservesColimit F (sheafCompose J AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor.{max u v r, r}) := by
  obtain ⟨_, _⟩ := hasSheafify_and_wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat.{u, v, r} J
  have := preservesSheafification_uliftFunctor.{u, v, r} J
  let Φ := AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor.{max u v r, r}
  let L₁ := presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{r}
  let P := F ⋙ sheafToPresheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{r}
  let cP := colimit.cocone P
  let hP := colimit.isColimit P
  let e : F ≅ P ⋙ L₁ :=
    Functor.isoWhiskerLeft F (asIso (sheafificationAdjunction J AddCommGrpCat.{r}).counit).symm
  let cF := (Cocone.precompose e.hom).obj (L₁.mapCocone cP)
  have hF : IsColimit cF := (IsColimit.precomposeHomEquiv e _).symm (isColimitOfPreserves L₁ hP)
  have hcomp : PreservesColimit P (L₁ ⋙ sheafCompose J Φ) := by
    have hiso : L₁ ⋙ sheafCompose J Φ ≅
        (Functor.whiskeringRight Cᵒᵖ AddCommGrpCat.{r} AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r}).obj Φ ⋙
          presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r} :=
      (sheafComposeNatIso J Φ (sheafificationAdjunction J AddCommGrpCat.{r})
        (sheafificationAdjunction J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r})).symm
    refine (preservesColimit_iff_of_natIso P hiso).mpr ?_
    infer_instance
  have hT := isColimitOfPreserves (L₁ ⋙ sheafCompose J Φ) hP
  let e' := Functor.isoWhiskerRight e (sheafCompose J Φ)
  have hT' : IsColimit ((Cocone.precompose e'.hom).obj
      ((L₁ ⋙ sheafCompose J Φ).mapCocone cP)) :=
    (IsColimit.precomposeHomEquiv e' _).symm hT
  have hMapF : IsColimit ((sheafCompose J Φ).mapCocone cF) := by
    apply IsColimit.ofIsoColimit hT'
    exact Cocone.ext (Iso.refl _) (by intro j; simp [cF, e'])
  exact preservesColimit_of_preserves_colimit_cocone hF hMapF

/-- **Raising the universe of the sections of a sheaf of modules preserves coproducts.** The
forgetful functor to abelian sheaves preserves coproducts and reflects isomorphisms, hence
reflects coproducts, and the lift of a sheaf of modules is the lift of the underlying abelian
sheaf. -/
theorem preservesColimitsOfShape_moduleULift (I : Type r) :
    PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete I) (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R) := by
  obtain ⟨_, _⟩ := hasSheafify_and_wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat.{u, v, r} J
  have h0 : PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete I) (_root_.SheafOfModules.toSheaf.{r} R) :=
    preservesColimitsOfShape_of_equiv
      ((ShrinkHoms.equivalence.{max u r} (Discrete I)).trans (Shrink.equivalence.{r} _)).symm _
  have h0' : PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete I)
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.toSheaf.{max u v r} R) :=
    preservesColimitsOfShape_of_equiv
      ((ShrinkHoms.equivalence.{max u (max u v r)} (Discrete I)).trans
        (Shrink.equivalence.{max u v r} _)).symm _
  have h1 : PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete I)
      (sheafCompose J AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor.{max u v r, r}) :=
    ⟨fun {F} => preservesColimit_sheafCompose_uliftFunctor I F⟩
  have h2 : PreservesColimitsOfShape (Discrete I)
      (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R ⋙ _root_.SheafOfModules.toSheaf.{max u v r} R) := by
    have he : moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R ⋙ _root_.SheafOfModules.toSheaf.{max u v r} R =
        _root_.SheafOfModules.toSheaf.{r} R ⋙
          sheafCompose J AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor.{max u v r, r} := rfl
    rw [he]
    infer_instance
  have h3 : ReflectsColimitsOfShape (Discrete I)
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.toSheaf.{max u v r} R) :=
    reflectsColimitsOfShape_of_reflectsIsomorphisms
  exact preservesColimitsOfShape_of_reflects_of_preserves _
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.toSheaf.{max u v r} R)

omit [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{r}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{r}] in
/-- Raising the universe of the sections of a sheaf of modules preserves finite limits: finite
limits of sheaves of modules are computed on the underlying presheaves of abelian groups, and
there the lift is postcomposition with `AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor`. -/
theorem preservesFiniteLimits_moduleULift :
    PreservesFiniteLimits (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R) := by
  let G := _root_.SheafOfModules.forget.{max u v r} R ⋙ PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R.obj
  have hG : PreservesFiniteLimits (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R ⋙ G) := by
    show PreservesFiniteLimits
      ((_root_.SheafOfModules.forget.{r} R ⋙ PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R.obj) ⋙
        (Functor.whiskeringRight Cᵒᵖ AddCommGrpCat.{r} AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r}).obj
          AddCommGrpCat.uliftFunctor.{max u v r, r})
    infer_instance
  exact preservesFiniteLimits_of_reflects_of_preserves (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R) G

/-- **The universe lift of a free sheaf of modules is a coproduct of copies of the universe lift
of the structure sheaf**, indexed by the `ULift` of the original index type.  This is the shape
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` asks of the two ends of a presentation. -/
noncomputable def isColimitCofanUliftForPresentationFree (I : Type r) :
    IsColimit (Cofan.mk
      (f := fun _ : ULift.{max u v r} I =>
        _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
          (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit R))
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.free I))
      fun j => _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.ιFree j.down)) := by
  have := preservesColimitsOfShape_moduleULift (R := R) I
  exact isColimitCofanULift ((Cofan.isColimitMapCoconeEquiv (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R) _
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.freeCofan I)).toFun
    (isColimitOfPreserves (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R)
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.isColimitFreeCofan I)))

/-! ### From a presentation to a global presentation -/

/-- An epimorphism of sheaves of modules is locally surjective on sections, with the strong
sheafification hypothesis that fact needs supplied from the weak one. -/
theorem epi_isLocallySurjective {M N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{r} R} (ψ : M ⟶ N)
    (h : Epi ψ) :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R.obj).map ψ.val) :=
  have : HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{r} :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.hasSheafify_of_locallyBijective
  have := h
  EpiMono.isLocallySurjective_of_epi ψ

variable {N : _root_.SheafOfModules.{r} R}

/-- The morphism between free sheaves of modules carried by a `SheafOfModules.Presentation`: the
generators of the kernel of the presenting morphism, followed by the inclusion of that
kernel. -/
noncomputable def presentationRelationsHom (P : N.Presentation) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := R) P.relations.I ⟶
      _root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := R) P.generators.I :=
  (_root_.SheafOfModules.freeHomEquiv (kernel P.generators.π)).symm P.relations.s ≫
    kernel.ι P.generators.π

/-- The two morphisms of a `SheafOfModules.Presentation` compose to zero. -/
theorem presentationRelationsHom_comp_generators_π (P : N.Presentation) :
    presentationRelationsHom P ≫ P.generators.π = 0 := by
  simp [presentationRelationsHom]

/-- The relations of a `SheafOfModules.Presentation` surject onto the kernel of its presenting
morphism: the lift of `Stacks.SheafOfModules.presentationRelationsHom` through that kernel is
the morphism generating it. -/
theorem epi_kernel_lift_presentationRelationsHom (P : N.Presentation) :
    Epi (kernel.lift P.generators.π (presentationRelationsHom P)
      (presentationRelationsHom_comp_generators_π P)) := by
  have h : kernel.lift P.generators.π (presentationRelationsHom P)
      (presentationRelationsHom_comp_generators_π P) =
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.freeHomEquiv (kernel P.generators.π)).symm P.relations.s := by
    rw [← cancel_mono (kernel.ι P.generators.π), kernel.lift_ι]
    rfl
  rw [h]
  exact P.relations.epi

/-- The universe lifts of the two morphisms of a `SheafOfModules.Presentation` compose to
zero. -/
theorem uliftForPresentationMap_presentationRelationsHom_comp (P : N.Presentation) :
    _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
        (presentationRelationsHom P) ≫
      _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
        P.generators.π = 0 := by
  rw [← _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap_comp,
    presentationRelationsHom_comp_generators_π]
  ext X x
  exact ULift.ext _ _ rfl

/-- **The universe lift of the presenting morphism of a `SheafOfModules.Presentation` is again a
cokernel projection.** The presenting morphism is locally surjective, being an epimorphism, and
every section it kills lies locally in the submodule generated by the relations, because the
relations surject onto its kernel. -/
noncomputable def isColimitCokernelCoforkPresentation (P : N.Presentation) :
    IsColimit (CokernelCofork.ofπ
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} P.generators.π)
      (uliftForPresentationMap_presentationRelationsHom_comp P)) := by
  have : HasSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r} :=
    GrothendieckTopology.hasSheafify_addCommGrpCat.{max u v r, v, u} J
  have : J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{max u v r} :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.SheafOfModules.wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat.{max u v r, u, v} J
  exact isColimitCokernelCoforkMapModuleULift.{max u v r, r, r, u, v} (presentationRelationsHom P)
    P.generators.π (presentationRelationsHom_comp_generators_π P)
    (epi_isLocallySurjective _ P.generators.epi)
    (mem_localClosure_of_epi_kernelLift _ _ _
      (epi_kernel_lift_presentationRelationsHom P) fun ψ h => epi_isLocallySurjective ψ h)

/-- **Stacks 03DL(6), from Mathlib's encoding to the universal-property one.** A sheaf of
modules admitting a `SheafOfModules.Presentation` admits a
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation`: the universe lift carries the presenting cokernel
diagram to a cokernel diagram, and it carries the two free sheaves of modules to coproducts of
copies of the lifted structure sheaf. -/
theorem hasGlobalPresentation_of_presentation (P : N.Presentation) :
    N.HasGlobalPresentation :=
  ⟨ULift.{max u v r} P.generators.I, ULift.{max u v r} P.relations.I, _, _, _, _,
    ⟨isColimitCofanUliftForPresentationFree P.generators.I⟩,
    ⟨isColimitCofanUliftForPresentationFree P.relations.I⟩,
    _, _, _, ⟨isColimitCokernelCoforkPresentation P⟩⟩

/-! ### From a global presentation to a presentation -/

/-- **Shrinking the index of a family of generating global sections.** A sheaf of modules that
receives an epimorphism from a coproduct of copies of the lifted structure sheaf is generated by
global sections indexed in the universe of the sections of the ring sheaf, as soon as its global
sections form a type in that universe: the index is replaced by the set of sections that the
structural inclusions name, and generation depends only on that set.

The comparison morphism `θ` out of the given coproduct is returned with the statement, because
it is an epimorphism and the presenting morphism factors through it; that is what carries the
relations along. -/
theorem exists_generatingSections_of_isColimit_cofan
    {M : _root_.SheafOfModules.{r} R} (hsmall : Small.{r} M.sections)
    {I : Type (max u v r)} {Pt : _root_.SheafOfModules.{max u v r} R}
    {ι : I → (_root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit R) ⟶ Pt)}
    (hPt : IsColimit (Cofan.mk Pt ι))
    (p : Pt ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} M)
    (hp : Epi p) :
    ∃ (G : M.GeneratingSections)
      (θ : Pt ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := R) G.I)),
      Epi θ ∧
        θ ≫ _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} G.π = p := by
  classical
  have := hsmall
  have := hp
  set σ : I → M.sections := fun i => uliftForPresentationSectionsEquiv M (ι i ≫ p) with hσ
  have hsub : Small.{r} {x : M.sections // x ∈ Set.range σ} := inferInstance
  set I' := Shrink.{r} {x : M.sections // x ∈ Set.range σ} with hI'
  set s' : I' → M.sections := fun k => ((equivShrink _).symm k).1 with hs'
  set c : I → I' := fun i => equivShrink _ ⟨σ i, ⟨i, rfl⟩⟩ with hc
  have hcs : ∀ i, s' (c i) = σ i := by
    intro i
    simp only [hs', hc, Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
  have hcsurj : ∀ k : I', ∃ i, c i = k := by
    intro k
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := ((equivShrink {x : M.sections // x ∈ Set.range σ}).symm k).2
    refine ⟨i, ?_⟩
    have hk : (⟨σ i, ⟨i, rfl⟩⟩ : {x : M.sections // x ∈ Set.range σ}) =
      (equivShrink {x : M.sections // x ∈ Set.range σ}).symm k := Subtype.ext hi
    simp only [hc, hk, Equiv.apply_symm_apply]
  set g : _root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := R) I' ⟶ M := M.freeHomEquiv.symm s' with hg
  set θ : Pt ⟶ _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentation.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
      (_root_.SheafOfModules.free (R := R) I') :=
    Cofan.IsColimit.desc hPt (fun i =>
      _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.ιFree (c i))) with hθ
  have hinj : ∀ i, (Cofan.mk Pt ι).inj i ≫ θ =
      _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.ιFree (c i)) := fun i => Cofan.IsColimit.fac hPt _ i
  have hfac : θ ≫ _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} g = p := by
    refine Cofan.IsColimit.hom_ext hPt _ _ fun i => ?_
    show (Cofan.mk Pt ι).inj i ≫ θ ≫ _ = (Cofan.mk Pt ι).inj i ≫ p
    rw [← Category.assoc, hinj i, ← _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap_comp]
    have h2 : _root_.SheafOfModules.ιFree (c i) ≫ g = M.unitHomEquiv.symm (σ i) := by
      rw [← hcs i, ← _root_.SheafOfModules.unitHomEquiv_symm_freeHomEquiv_apply g (c i), hg,
        Equiv.apply_symm_apply]
    have h3 : M.unitHomEquiv.symm (σ i) =
        (uliftForPresentationHomEquiv (_root_.SheafOfModules.unit R) M).symm (ι i ≫ p) := by
      simp only [hσ, uliftForPresentationSectionsEquiv, Equiv.trans_apply,
        Equiv.symm_apply_apply]
    rw [h2, h3]
    exact (uliftForPresentationHomEquiv _ M).apply_symm_apply (ι i ≫ p)
  have hθepi : Epi θ := by
    refine ⟨fun ψ₁ ψ₂ hψ => ?_⟩
    refine Cofan.IsColimit.hom_ext (isColimitCofanUliftForPresentationFree (R := R) I') _ _
      fun j => ?_
    obtain ⟨i, hi⟩ := hcsurj j.down
    have h4 : _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.ιFree (R := R) j.down) = (Cofan.mk Pt ι).inj i ≫ θ := by
      rw [hinj i, hi]
    show _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.ιFree (R := R) j.down) ≫ ψ₁ =
      _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r}
        (_root_.SheafOfModules.ιFree (R := R) j.down) ≫ ψ₂
    rw [h4, Category.assoc, hψ, Category.assoc]
  have hgepi : Epi (_root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} g) :=
    epi_of_epi_fac hfac
  have : (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R).Faithful :=
    (moduleULiftFullyFaithful.{max u v r, r} R).faithful
  have : (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R).ReflectsEpimorphisms :=
    Functor.reflectsEpimorphisms_of_faithful _
  have hg' : Epi g := (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R).epi_of_epi_map hgepi
  rw [hg] at hg'
  exact ⟨{ I := I', s := s', epi := hg' }, θ, hθepi, hfac⟩

/-- **Stacks 03DL(6), from the universal-property encoding to Mathlib's.** On a site that is
essentially small in the universe of the sections of the ring sheaf, a sheaf of modules with a
`SheafOfModules.HasGlobalPresentation` has a `SheafOfModules.Presentation`.

The structural inclusions of the presenting coproduct name global sections of the module, and
the set of sections they name is a type in the universe of the sections, which makes it an
admissible index type; after that replacement the presenting morphism is still a cokernel, now
of the original relations composed with the comparison morphism, so the relation coproduct still
surjects onto the new kernel and the same replacement applies to it. -/
theorem nonempty_presentation_of_hasGlobalPresentation [EssentiallySmall.{r} C]
    (h : N.HasGlobalPresentation) : Nonempty N.Presentation := by
  obtain ⟨_, _⟩ := hasSheafify_and_wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrpCat.{u, v, r} J
  obtain ⟨I, K, Pt, Q, ι, κ, ⟨hPt⟩, ⟨hQ⟩, a, b, hab, ⟨hcok⟩⟩ := h
  have hbepi : Epi b := Cofork.IsColimit.epi hcok
  obtain ⟨G, θ, hθepi, hfac⟩ :=
    exists_generatingSections_of_isColimit_cofan (small_sections N) hPt b hbepi
  have hπepi : Epi (_root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} G.π) :=
    epi_of_epi_fac hfac
  have hz : (a ≫ θ) ≫
      _root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} G.π = 0 := by
    rw [Category.assoc, hfac]; exact hab
  have hck := isColimitCokernelCoforkOfEpiComp hab hcok hfac hz
  let S := ShortComplex.mk (a ≫ θ)
    (_root_.SheafOfModules.uliftForPresentationMap.{u, v, r, r, max u v r} G.π) hz
  have hSex : S.Exact := ShortComplex.exact_of_g_is_cokernel S hck
  have hlift : Epi (kernel.lift S.g S.f S.zero) := hSex.epi_kernelLift
  have := preservesFiniteLimits_moduleULift.{u, v, r} (R := R)
  have hkiso : IsIso (PreservesKernel.iso (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R) G.π).inv :=
    Iso.isIso_inv _
  have hkinv : Epi (PreservesKernel.iso (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R) G.π).inv :=
    IsSplitEpi.epi _
  have hpQ : Epi (kernel.lift S.g S.f S.zero ≫
      (PreservesKernel.iso (moduleULift.{max u v r, r} R) G.π).inv) :=
    @epi_comp _ _ _ _ _ _ hlift _ hkinv
  obtain ⟨Grel, -⟩ := exists_generatingSections_of_isColimit_cofan
    (small_sections (kernel G.π)) hQ _ hpQ
  exact ⟨⟨G, Grel⟩⟩

/-- **The two encodings of Stacks 03DL(6) agree** on a site that is essentially small in the
universe of the sections of the ring sheaf. -/
theorem nonempty_presentation_iff_hasGlobalPresentation [EssentiallySmall.{r} C] :
    Nonempty N.Presentation ↔ N.HasGlobalPresentation :=
  ⟨fun h => h.elim hasGlobalPresentation_of_presentation,
    nonempty_presentation_of_hasGlobalPresentation⟩

end Stacks.SheafOfModules

end
